   - LL-integrals:     1
   - LS-integrals:     0
   - SS-integrals:     0
   - GT-integrals:     0
 * Basis set:
   - uncontracted large component basis set
   - uncontracted small component basis set


 Information about the restricted kinetic balance scheme:
 * Default RKB projection:
   1: Pre-projection in scalar basis
   2: Removal of unphysical solutions (via diagonalization of free particle Hamiltonian)
 File with embedding potentia (=fdepot) is EMBPOT                                                      
 File with frozen density (+gradient etc) (=fdedns) is FRZDN1                                                      
* Kohn-Sham calculation using the automatic differentiation xc functional:
   (weight: functional)
  1.000000: kin_tf

  
 =====================================================================================================
 Frozen Density Embedding to include enviroment effects using the fixed potential method described in:
 A.S.P. Gomes, C. R. Jacob and L. Visscher, Phys. Chem. Chem. Phys. 10 (2008) 5353–5362.
 =====================================================================================================

  Frozen Density Embedding Calculation set-up:
  --------------------------------------------

 * Print level:     0
 * FDE Potential read from file: EMBPOT                                                      
 * Density (and gradient) from frozen subsystems read from file: FRZDN1                                                      


   Kohn-Sham calculation set-up
   ----------------------------

 * Print level:     2
 * Numerical integration grid:
   - radial quadrature according to R. Lindh, P.-Aa. Malmqvist, and L. Gagliardi
     precision of radial quadrature set to:  0.10000E-12
   - angular quadrature using the Lebedev scheme, exact up to order L = 41
   - accepted error in integrated number of electrons:  0.10000E-02
 * DFT thresholds:
   - dfthr0 =  0.10000E-08
   - dfthri =  0.20000E-11
 * Spin density contribution in response calculations:
   - use the norm of the spin magnetization vector as a definition of the spin density (noncollinear definition)
 * Adiabatic local density approximation (ALDA):
   - approximate all functional derivatives beyond the xc potential by SVWN derivatives
   - for hybrid functionals exact exchange is switched off in the solution of the response equation
     (if you want to keep it, use .XALDA)


